I'm sure you've heard all about horse  balls at this point but as it turns out  horses play a much bigger role in Red  Dead Redemption too than you might think  so much so that it can be overwhelming  if you haven't been paying close  attention to the tutorial messages I'm  gonna try to answer all your horse  related questions in this spoiler free  video so let's start from the beginning  horse controls are relatively simple  depending on what console you're playing  on tap a or X repeatedly to speed up and  r1 or RB to slow down you can double tap  and hold X or a to match a companion  speed and if you tap a or X and rhythm  with your horses gallop you will  conserve stamina as you ride your horse  you'll want to keep an eye on it scores  the heart is the health obviously and  the lightning bolt is stamina the more  you push your horse the quicker the  stamina bar will deplete and if you  don't feed your horse every now and then  or let it rest its core will drain and  it won't have as much stamina or health  meaning this will happen as you ride  feed and clean your horse your bond will  strengthen and as that bond grows you're  worse will learn advanced maneuvers at  level 2 you can rear your horse back by  pressing r1 or RB with square or X I  haven't really found a use for this  other than to look threatening from time  to time at level 3 you learn how to skip  [Music]  while sprinting press r1 or RB and you  can either bring your horse to a halt  or change directions at a moment's  notice finally at level 4 you learn how  to drift in piaf which is a fancy word  for strafe as your bond increases your  horse will also respond to your call  from greater and greater distances and  its stats including speed will also get  a slight bump if you want to see how  close your horse is to the next level  you can check the player menu when you  hit start however if you want to get the  most out of your horse you want to stop  at a stable and upgraded saddle most  items for sale are cosmetics however  there are a few things that can improve  your horse - stats like the stirrups and  the saddles themselves but wait you say  I can't seem to enter the stable and I  can't find a stupid brush to clean my  horse well that probably means you're  screwing off too much and not doing  story missions  once you complete an early mission  called exit pursued by a bruised ego you  will have access to stables across the  map and you will get a nifty brush while  at the stables you can also rename sell  and buy horses you can sell both stolen  horses and horses you've acquired  legally stolen horses won't fetch as  good of a price at stables but at a  certain point the story you will meet  some characters willing to purchase  stolen horses for a better profit heard  you paid good prices for horses level  for horses will also fetch a higher  price so if you plan on flipping a horse  I'd recommend leveling it up first  if you are looking to buy a horse the  first thing you'll probably notice is  that good horses and cheap as much as I  love tiny here he's not exactly the  powerhouse you want by your side  throughout the entire game and if the  best horses are too expensive I guess  that means we'll have to break them  ourselves lucky for you one of the best  horses in the game can be acquired for  free at the beginning of chapter two and  onward but before we get to that let's  learn how to break a horse as you  explore the world you'll find horses  everywhere big horses little horses  painted horses black horses and so on  there are a dozen different breeds  roaming the frontier all with unique  stats and attributes if you see a horse  you're interested in first take out your  binoculars once you study the horse you  will be given a prompt to show info hit  that and you can check out the horses  stats and its breed  details now there are two ways to go  about breaking a horse you can chase it  down lasso it and hop on its back or you  can approach it slowly calming it if it  gets spooked once you get close enough  you can hop on based on my extensive  research I can say with confidence that  it's much easier to break a horse if you  approach it slowly once you're on it  pull back the left stick and subtly tilt  the right stick to balance wall calming  it with square or X if it bucks you  which it probably will at first chase it  down when it calms down a bit you can  repeat the process also be mindful of  its friends  once you feel comfortable breaking  horses pack yourself some warm clothes  and head up to the Grizzlies right next  to this Lake a white coat Arabian spawns  it can be a slippery bastard but it's  well worth the effort if it bucks you  and escapes well it's gonna be a while  before another one responds so I  wouldn't wait around once you do break  it put a saddle on it and take it to the  nearest stable technically the horse  will be yours once you put the saddle on  but I like to take it back to the stable  just in case there are two other  extremely rare wild horses you can break  but finding them takes a bit longer so  maybe we'll save that for another video  a couple more things to note before I  close out this video if your horse gets  too dirty its meters will drain 25%  quicker you can clean it with your brush  or by riding it through clean water you  can expedite bonding by petting your  horse and feeding it treats your horses  cores will refill if you sleep and the  stronger your bond is with a horse the  longer it will take to bleed out if it  gets knocked down  a level four horse will take sixty  minutes before it dies giving you plenty  of time to get to town and purchase a  horse survivor good luck out there in  the wild and remember whether you're an  honorable gunslinger or a dishonorable  outlaw you should always pet your loyal  horse from time to time if you want more  Red Dead to content you should check out  our new show dirty RT where we see how  disgusting we can make Arthur Morgan  thank you for watching all right I guess  I didn't quite fit under there
 

